+# v14: audited corrections, experimental checkpoint
+
+Based on 9888780 (v13 plus the other agent's smoke fixture restoration).
+This is not a clean full-regression or Vulkan-conformance milestone.
+
+## Driver changes
+
+- Clear exactly three words per 12-byte TASK record. The previous fourth word
+  could overwrite the next record or the first payload in a full chunk.
+- Use flat local invocation index zero for the record initializer and TASK
+  statistics writer; add the API local workgroup size to the query counter.
+- Restore the MESH API invocation multiplier and add missing query accounting
+  when API workgroup size equals hardware workgroup size. The new local-size-32
+  regression returned 0 instead of 192 before the latter fix, then passed.
+- Wait for graphics readers before reusing record/payload scratch between chunks.
+  This deliberately favors correctness over throughput; cost is not benchmarked.
+- Preserve CullPrimitive's per-primitive array/type/index through expansion.
+- Correct the maxDrawIndirectCount comment (independent of EXT_multi_draw).
+
+The MESH query compiler changes affect the common AMD mesh path, not only BC250.
+Other GPU models were not tested.
+
+## Harness changes
+
+Explicit device query features, initial host reset of every query pool, and reset
+availability assertions replace invalid feature combinations and numerical-zero
+assumptions. Shader draw parameters are enabled for DrawID tests. The boundary
+harness enables mesh-stage storage atomics and indirect-count where used.
+
+Runners use fresh default directories, preserve shader/hash/compile provenance,
+validate SPIR-V, and fail on unexpected process status. Phase markers distinguish
+preparing from launching. A timeout does not stop a hung GPU. Explicit result
+paths must be new; never borrow stale SPIR-V for a manual probe.
+
+`run-v14-focused.sh` runs three local-size cases (32x1x1, 2x4x4, 1x4x6), nine
+axis/direct/indirect/indirect-count boundary cases, and expanded CullPrimitive.
+Each boundary test checks 8194 unique TASK identities, each consumed twice;
+expected invocation totals are TASK=262208 and MESH=524416. A host-visible buffer
+checks every identity, builtins, payload sentinel and an end guard. This remains
+limited to the tested payload and dispatch shapes, with one indirect record.
+
+`run-v14-cts.sh` contains seven exact selected official query/attribute cases.
+It requires exactly one passing case per invocation. It was prepared but NOT RUN
+in this session because validation stopped earlier.
+
+## Recorded results
+
+Evidence root: /home/quentin/bc250-codex/v14-validation
+
+- Initial isolated build passed.
+- `query.log`: all 14 corrected custom modes passed on the first v14 candidate
+  before the missing full-workgroup MESH counter was fixed.
+- `focused.log`: intentionally retained failure showing the missing counter.
+- `focused2.log`: all 13 focused cases passed on the final driver binary.
+- `hybrid.log`: initial candidate passed native mesh, cull, basic/multiple TASK,
+  skip, fanout and atomic-payload checks. Board became unreachable afterward.
+  Marker said task-repeat, but no task-repeat log/archive exists; submission of
+  that next case is not established.
+- `final-query.log`: final binary passed hw, combined, mesh, task and both.
+  Board became unreachable before query-chunked produced a log/archive. The
+  official CTS and full expansion/compaction stages therefore never started.
+- User power-cycled twice. Exact cause of interruptions remains unknown.
+
+Final driver SHA256 (same binary as focused2):
+7a15489f4e2e6f7362afe4cd06b0ffabdf92a4f212ed71d651252e09801f4cba
+
+Final runner phase/status additions received shell syntax and CPU compilation
+checks; no additional GPU run was made after the second recovery. Khronos
+validation layers were not installed in the inspected system layer directory,
+so do not claim a validation-layer-clean run.
+
+## Continue
+
+Preserve v3+ and existing game launchers. Original repository/build is untouched;
+v14 uses /home/quentin/bc250-codex/mesa-v14 on branch bc250-v14.
+
+Inspect both interrupted runs before more GPU work. Do not rerun either sequence
+unchanged or diagnose hardware from lost SSH. Investigate delayed completion,
+query/GDS lifetime and process teardown with a new bounded hypothesis, preserving
+system logs and phase markers. Then run the selected official CTS and remaining
+rendering suites. Do not silently upgrade Steam to this checkpoint.
+
+Remaining limitations include raw/large output handling, expansion capacity,
+feature-off queries, broader descriptor/lifecycle/payload cases, and the cost of
+1024 command pairs per indirect record. No new game or performance evidence.
