+# BC250 revision 4: experimental primitive-attribute expansion
+
+Revision 4 implements an opt-in compiler fallback for live generic per-primitive
+mesh attributes. It preserves the revision 3 hardware export guard and working
+checkpoint. System Mesa is unchanged; nothing has been published or pushed.
+
+## Implementation
+
+Set `RADV_BC250_EXPAND_PRIMITIVES=1` with the private development ICD. Add
+`RADV_BC250_HYBRID_TASK=1` for COMPUTE-backed TASK support.
+
+The original mesh program writes its output arrays into shared staging memory.
+A workgroup barrier precedes an epilogue that gives each primitive private
+vertices, copies its referenced vertex data, and copies its primitive attributes
+into flat per-vertex attributes. Fragment inputs are converted to match before
+shader linking. Shared application vertices can therefore carry different
+primitive colors without conflicts. Only referenced vertices are exported.
+
+The fallback setting is included in the compiler cache key. The original export
+guard remains in the common binding path. Disabling expansion, or encountering
+a shader outside its limits, leaves unsupported live exports guarded.
+
+Limits: at most 256 expanded vertices (85 triangles), a conservative 16 KiB
+shared-staging budget including existing shared allocation, paired mesh and
+fragment NIR, and generic primitive attributes. Built-in primitive routing and
+NV mesh shaders are excluded. Points and lines have generalized implementation
+paths but were not validated in this revision. Triangle workloads are the tested
+scope. Vertex duplication increases memory use and may reduce performance.
+
+This is a compiler fallback, not a demonstrated repair of the direct hardware
+per-primitive parameter-cache ABI. Mesa's GFX10.3 register definitions contain
+the relevant primitive parameter count fields while its GFX10 definitions do
+not; this evidence does not establish the BC250's complete hardware capability.
+
+## Hardware validation
+
+- Original guarded custom suite: **28 passing pixel/buffer readbacks**, with
+  expected rejection checks still passing.
+- New expansion suite: **41 passing pixel readbacks**, **two expected guarded
+  rejections**, and **ten byte-identical image comparisons** (eight expanded vs.
+  hand-expanded references plus two cache comparisons).
+- Native shared-vertex meshes: one/two groups, 32/128 invocations, compact and
+  sparse 256-vertex source arrays. Each native result matches its compact
+  hand-expanded reference byte for byte.
+- TASK: separate X/Y/Z groups, replay, and empty mesh groups at 32/128 invocations.
+  The original failing reproducer now renders 495 red and 495 green pixels.
+- Normal vertex controls repeatedly render 968 red pixels after experimental
+  workloads. No reboot or recovery was needed during this continuation.
+- Cache on/off/on: expansion renders, disabled expansion fails finalization
+  before submission, and reenabled expansion renders the same image.
+- An 86-triangle declared maximum exceeds the expansion budget and is rejected
+  before submission.
+
+Unmodified official CTS commit `659bbe6987197b4ff7ac20011261b92009286100`:
+
+| Selected coverage | Pass | Fail | Unsupported |
+|---|---:|---:|---:|
+| Smoke, excluding known invalid output-order case | 10 | 0 | 2 |
+| Payload access and task/mesh workgroup barriers | 24 | 0 | 0 |
+| TASK-to-MESH storage buffer/image synchronization | 6 | 0 | 0 |
+| Transfer-to-TASK buffer, sampled/storage image synchronization | 10 | 0 | 0 |
+| Total selected official cases | 50 | 0 | 2 |
+
+The unmodified `partial_usage` case is among the smoke passes. These selected
+results are not full Vulkan conformance or broad application validation.
+
+Separately, `partial_usage_without_compaction` **passes with the sole CTS
+correction moving SetMeshOutputsEXT before unused output writes**. The patch
+is included separately. It changes no colors, dispatches, or expected images.
+That modified result is not counted in the official total. Original CTS source
+was restored and rebuilt; a separate diagnostic executable remains remote.
+
+## Reproduce
+
