+# BC250 v5: compact sparse vertex-only output
+
+V5 extends the working v4 output-expansion fallback to vertex-only mesh shaders
+when expanding referenced primitives reduces the declared vertex capacity.
+Enable it with `RADV_BC250_EXPAND_PRIMITIVES=1`; TASK additionally requires
+`RADV_BC250_HYBRID_TASK=1`. System Mesa and the saved v3/v4 checkpoints remain
+unchanged.
+
+The original program writes shared staging arrays. The existing epilogue exports
+only referenced vertices, duplicating them where needed. V4 applied this to
+generic per-primitive attributes; v5 also applies it to sparse vertex-only output.
+It is a practical compiler workaround, not a repair of the hardware export ABI.
+The same 256-expanded-vertex and 16 KiB staging limits apply.
+
+## Investigation
+
+Raw, fully defined vertex output passed at 32, 64, 128 and 256 declared vertices
+with 32 API invocations. A small 256-output case failed with 64 invocations and
+was followed by loss of board responsiveness despite a passing immediate vertex
+control. Forcing wave32 also failed. A narrowly scoped explicit LDS-barrier-wait
+experiment compiled but did not fix rendering; it was reverted and v4 rebuilt.
+No wave-size change or ACO barrier modification is retained.
+
+Several recovery cycles were needed during raw-path investigation. The first
+interrupted full CTS rerun left an empty new wrapper log and an older case log;
+that stale result must not be counted. The actual root cause remains unresolved.
+Further raw-path testing needs a new explanation and controlled recovery.
+
+## Validation
+
+The new `run-native-compact.sh` verifies 19 pixel readbacks and six byte-identical
+comparisons against compact reference meshes: 32/64/128 API invocations, one/two
+native groups, and sparse 256-vertex source output. The previously failing
+64-invocation case passes through the new fallback.
+
+The specification-order-corrected CTS unused-vertex workload, additionally using
+per-vertex colors, passes in both native-only and TASK modes. These are separately
+modified diagnostics, not official conformance results. Their exact saved patch
+is included. Original CTS source is restored and rebuilt afterward.
+
+The original 28-readback suite and v4's 41-readback expansion suite also pass:
+88 passing readbacks across the three suites. The same 52 selected original CTS
+cases were rerun: 50 passes, zero failures and two unsupported shading-rate cases.
+Selected CTS coverage is not full conformance.
+
+## Reproduce
+
+```sh
+cd /home/quentin/bc250-codex
+export PATH="$HOME/bc250-codex/tools/bin:$PATH"
+ninja -C mesa/build -j4
+bash mesa/tests/bc250-native-mesh/run-native-compact.sh
+bash mesa/tests/bc250-native-mesh/run-hybrid.sh
+bash mesa/tests/bc250-native-mesh/run-expand.sh
+```
+
+The new runner creates its own private ICD. It does not execute the failing
+uncompacted 64-invocation case. Its artifacts are git-ignored under
+`tests/bc250-native-mesh/native-compact-results/`; logs also live under
+`/home/quentin/bc250-codex/logs/native-compact/`.
+
+Apply the incremental patch to exact v4 commit
+`03fad29d5ee294cd618ba492e24adb93e2d097b6`. Keep the v4 package as its prerequisite.
+Direct per-primitive exports remain guarded; raw large-output behavior, larger
+expansion budgets, CullPrimitive, full descriptor/lifecycle coverage, queries,
+and the below-minimum TASK workgroup cap remain open. The user accepts practical
+board-specific workarounds; prioritize working, repeatably validated behavior.
